#: ../../BaTiO3/stability.rst:5
msgid "安定基底状態"
msgstr "Stable Ground State"

#: ../../BaTiO3/stability.rst:7
msgid ""
"BaTiO₃ の 4 つの結晶相のうち、0 K で最もエネルギーが低いのはどの相でしょうか。\\ "
"各相の最適化済みの格子を使い、原子座標を緩和して全エネルギーを比較します。\\ 今回の DFT "
"と機械学習原子間ポテンシャル（MLIP）の計算では、5 手法すべてで菱面体晶が最も低く、斜方晶、正方晶、立方晶の順に高くなりました。\\ "
"菱面体晶と斜方晶の差は手法によっては 1 化学式単位あたり 1 meV 未満で、計算の収束条件に敏感です。"
msgstr ""
"Which of the four crystal phases of BaTiO₃ has the lowest energy at 0 K? "
"\\  We relax the atomic coordinates at the optimized lattice of each "
"phase and compare the total energies. \\  In our DFT and machine-learning"
" interatomic potential (MLIP) calculations, all five methods gave the "
"lowest energy for the rhombohedral phase, followed in increasing order by"
" the orthorhombic, tetragonal, and cubic phases. \\  For some methods, "
"the difference between the rhombohedral and orthorhombic phases is less "
"than 1 meV per formula unit and is sensitive to the convergence settings."

#: ../../BaTiO3/stability.rst:14
msgid "BaTiO₃ の分極方向は、低温側から菱面体晶で〈111〉、斜方晶で〈110〉、正方晶で〈100〉。立方晶は非極性。"
msgstr ""
"Polarization directions in BaTiO₃ from low to high temperatures are 〈111〉"
" in the rhombohedral phase, 〈110〉 in the orthorhombic phase, and 〈100〉 in"
" the tetragonal phase. The cubic phase is nonpolar."

#: ../../BaTiO3/stability.rst:19
msgid "BaTiO₃ の温度依存相系列と分極方向の概略図。Shu と Bhattacharya による整理に基づきます :sup:`[1]`。"
msgstr ""
"Schematic of the temperature-dependent phase sequence and polarization "
"directions of BaTiO₃, based on the phase sequence described by Shu and "
"Bhattacharya :sup:`[1]`."

#: ../../BaTiO3/stability.rst:21
msgid ""
"正方晶、斜方晶、菱面体晶の結晶構造や原子変位は、X 線・中性子回折などで調べられてきました :sup:`[2,3]`。\\ "
"第一原理計算に基づく有効ハミルトニアン研究では、局所的な極性ひずみと長距離相互作用の競合から、低温での安定性と相転移の順序が再現されています "
":sup:`[4,5]`。\\ 以下では、菱面体晶、斜方晶、正方晶、立方晶をそれぞれ "
":math:`R`、:math:`O`、:math:`T`、:math:`C` と書きます。\\ 4 相の空間群と分極の向きは、技術ノートの\\ "
"`4つの相と分極の向き <https://technical-"
"notes.quemix.com/solid/ferroelectricity.html#batio3-four-phases>`__\\ "
"にまとめました。"
msgstr ""
"X-ray and neutron diffraction, among other techniques, have been used to "
"study the crystal structures and atomic displacements of the tetragonal, "
"orthorhombic, and rhombohedral phases :sup:`[2,3]`. \\  Effective-"
"Hamiltonian studies based on first-principles calculations have "
"reproduced the low-temperature stability and phase transition sequence "
"from the competition between local polar distortions and long-range "
"interactions :sup:`[4,5]`. \\  Below, we denote the rhombohedral, "
"orthorhombic, tetragonal, and cubic phases by :math:`R`, :math:`O`, "
":math:`T`, and :math:`C`, respectively. \\  The Technical Notes section "
"on \\  `the four phases and their polarization directions <https"
"://technical-notes.quemix.com/solid/ferroelectricity.html#batio3-four-"
"phases>`__ \\  lists the space groups and polarization directions."

#: ../../BaTiO3/stability.rst:29
msgid "計算手順と代表的な入力ファイル"
msgstr "Calculation Procedure and Representative Input Files"

#: ../../BaTiO3/stability.rst:31
msgid ":doc:`lattice-constant` の手順に従い、各相の格子定数を最適化します。"
msgstr ""
"Optimize the lattice constants of each phase as described in :doc"
":`lattice-constant`."

#: ../../BaTiO3/stability.rst:32
msgid "最適化した格子を固定し、原子座標を緩和します。"
msgstr "Keep the optimized lattice fixed and relax the atomic coordinates."

#: ../../BaTiO3/stability.rst:33
msgid ""
"最終構造の全エネルギーを 1 化学式単位あたりに換算します。手法ごとに菱面体晶の値を差し引き、相対エネルギーを求めます（技術ノートの\\ "
"`化学式単位あたりの相対エネルギー <https://technical-"
"notes.quemix.com/electronic/pseudopotential_basis.html#energy-"
"reference>`__）。"
msgstr ""
"Convert the total energy of the final structure to energy per formula "
"unit. For each method, subtract the value for the rhombohedral phase to "
"obtain the relative energy (see the Technical Notes on \\  `relative "
"energy per formula unit <https://technical-"
"notes.quemix.com/electronic/pseudopotential_basis.html#energy-"
"reference>`__)."

#: ../../BaTiO3/stability.rst:35
msgid ""
"ここでは、構造最適化に用いた代表例として QE の入力ファイルのみを示します。\\ Quloud Job では、各相のジョブに含まれる "
"``QuloudJob.scf.in`` を以下の例で\\ 置き換えることで、同じ形式の固定格子構造最適化を実行できます。入力中の\\ "
"``calculation = 'relax'`` は格子を固定して原子位置のみを最適化する指定（`固定セル緩和 <https"
"://technical-notes.quemix.com/electronic/structure_optimization.html"
"#structure-optimization>`__）であり、\\ ``ibrav``、``A``、``B``、``C``、``cosAB`` "
"には、直前の格子最適化で得られた\\ 各相の格子定数を用いています。原子位置の固定フラグは付けていないため、\\ Ti と O "
"を含む内部座標は最適化されます。"
msgstr ""
"Of the inputs used for geometry optimization, we show only the QE input "
"files as representative examples here. \\  In a Quloud Job, replacing "
"``QuloudJob.scf.in`` for a given phase with the corresponding example "
"below \\  lets you run the same type of fixed-lattice geometry "
"optimization. The setting \\  ``calculation = 'relax'`` optimizes only "
"the atomic positions at a fixed lattice (see `fixed-cell relaxation "
"<https://technical-"
"notes.quemix.com/electronic/structure_optimization.html#structure-"
"optimization>`__). The parameters \\  ``ibrav``, ``A``, ``B``, ``C``, and"
" ``cosAB`` use the lattice constants \\  obtained for each phase in the "
"preceding lattice optimization. With no flags to fix the atomic "
"positions, \\  the internal coordinates, including those of Ti and O, are"
" optimized."

